WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
An attack on a Katari LNG tanker in the Gulf raises risks to energy shipments that millions rely on for power and transport. This is Omni View, Episode 223. Indian opposition crowds filled Delhi over voter rolls, Yemeni government forces push an al-Jouth, Ukrainian grain moves under renewed fire, and later a week in review. The al-Maheda, owned by Katar Gas Transport Company, was struck by unidentified objects Friday evening while sailing in the Gulf. The company supplies Katari Port

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.980
reports and terminals with towage and marine support services.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.040
No crew members were injured and no environmental damage was reported.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:41.900
A statement published by the Qatar Stock Exchange said the vessel is currently in a safe

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:46.160
condition and operational, and that the impact of the incident is being assessed.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:52.040
Al-Jazeera reports the incident as the latest in more than 120 commercial ship attacks since

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:54.800
the U.S.-Israel war on Iran began in February.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:01.000
That reporting says October was the worst month of the war, with 29 ships hit, ahead of

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.660
the 20 attacks recorded in March.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:07.820
Iran has warned vessels passing the Strait of Hormuz without permission, and the same

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:12.600
account links the rise in attacks to a U.S. blockade on Iranian ports imposed in July.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:18.660
The carrier was transporting cargo bound for Pakistan, and Bloomberg reports that negotiations

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:23.560
with Iran had secured prior approval for safe passage for the specific cargo before the

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:28.560
strike occurred. The Qatar Gas Transport Company statement confirms the carrier supplies

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.620
liquefied natural gas and points to tracking by the International Maritime Organization

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:40.845
or IMO and the UK Maritime Trade Operations. Thousands gathered in Delhi on Sunday demanding

00:01:40.845 --> 00:01:46.405
the resignation of India's election chief after a revision of voter lists. The South China Morning

00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:52.325
Post reports the opposition, led by Congress Party Chief Rahul Gandhi, argues the change's

00:01:52.325 --> 00:01:58.705
favor Prime Minister Narendra Modi's Baratia Janata party, or BJP. Those protests form

00:01:58.705 --> 00:02:03.105
part of more than a month of opposition demonstrations challenging the electoral process.

00:02:03.765 --> 00:02:08.125
Sunday's protesters say the controversial revision benefits Modi's Hindu nationalist

00:02:08.125 --> 00:02:13.865
BJP, and they want the election chief out on that basis. Gandhi's Congress Party treats

00:02:13.865 --> 00:02:18.645
the revision as a change that tilts the contest toward the ruling party, not as a routine

00:02:18.645 --> 00:02:23.405
clean up of the roles. The same reporting frames the demonstrations as the worst crisis

00:02:23.405 --> 00:02:28.645
for Modi since he took office. Analysts cited their view the growing support for the opposition

00:02:28.645 --> 00:02:32.265
as a significant political development in the world's largest democracy.

00:02:33.369 --> 00:02:37.869
Yemen's internationally recognized government announced its forces seized military positions

00:02:37.869 --> 00:02:44.609
and strategic heights east of Al-Hazam, the capital of Al-Jauf governorate. Al-Jazira places the

00:02:44.609 --> 00:02:48.669
advance with an Operation Dawn of Yemen, launched in October to reverse

00:02:48.669 --> 00:02:53.489
Houthi territorial gains. The first emergency brigade reported capturing weapons

00:02:53.489 --> 00:02:57.989
and ammunition depots while destroying armored vehicles after wounding, killing

00:02:57.989 --> 00:03:03.229
and capturing Houthi fighters. The Army's media center said in a post on X on Saturday

00:03:03.229 --> 00:03:07.169
that the attacks resulted in the destruction of armored vehicles. The

00:03:07.169 --> 00:03:11.809
Governorate border Saudi Arabia and lies near Houthi held areas, making it a

00:03:11.809 --> 00:03:16.269
key front. Whether those heights have actually changed hands is contested in the field.

00:03:16.809 --> 00:03:21.269
The Houthis said they had thwarted advances by government forces in Al-Jauf and neighboring

00:03:21.269 --> 00:03:27.649
Marib. Fighting also continues around the besiege city of Tayez, where more than 290,000

00:03:27.649 --> 00:03:31.849
people have fled since August, according to the United Nations Office for the coordination

00:03:31.849 --> 00:03:37.709
of humanitarian affairs. The siege strains hospitals and restricts deliveries of food, fuel,

00:03:37.709 --> 00:03:42.289
and medical supplies. Videos published by Yemeni media showed what the outlets

00:03:42.289 --> 00:03:46.189
described as the first shipment of medical aid arriving from Mariebe to support

00:03:46.189 --> 00:03:51.610
wounded people, displaced families, and other residents. Ukrainian farmers keep

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:55.370
working their export routes as Russian forces have renewed attacks on grain

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:59.910
shipments. The Christian Science Monitor reports those attacks now combine drone

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:04.870
strikes with rising diesel prices that strain the agricultural sector. Direct hits

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:09.550
It's on ports sit alongside higher fuel costs, and that reporting says the whole industry

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:10.210
is strained.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:15.350
Ukraine's agricultural exports remain a major global food supply route, despite the added

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:16.390
risks to shipments.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:22.650
Farmers continue operations, even so, with agricultural exports under fire from Russia once again.

00:04:23.618 --> 00:04:28.178
Policy tools for China's capital market go on the table Monday when the central bank and

00:04:28.178 --> 00:04:31.958
the securities regulator convene, according to local media reports.

00:04:31.958 --> 00:04:37.458
Blumberg reports the meeting comes as authorities seek measures to stabilize markets amid ongoing

00:04:37.458 --> 00:04:38.518
economic pressures.

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:43.278
The two bodies will examine available tools designed to support the country's capital

00:04:43.278 --> 00:04:46.698
market and address those pressures through specific policy measures.

00:04:47.633 --> 00:04:52.133
Rising fuel costs linked to geopolitical tensions in the Middle East are hitting Canada's

00:04:52.133 --> 00:04:52.473
airlines.

00:04:53.173 --> 00:04:58.113
SSB crack reports the cost increases are affecting operations across the sector as airlines

00:04:58.113 --> 00:05:00.953
adjust to higher prices driven by regional developments.

00:05:00.953 --> 00:05:06.002
payments. Bangladesh is pushing in the right direction, forming a wage board after garment

00:05:06.002 --> 00:05:11.002
workers protested rising living costs. Al Jazeera reports the board was established

00:05:11.002 --> 00:05:16.442
amid ongoing protests by workers seeking higher pay. Demonstrations took place in industrial

00:05:16.442 --> 00:05:21.262
cities as workers sought that higher pay. The move represents a formal government response

00:05:21.262 --> 00:05:27.554
to the demonstrations in industrial areas. Elsewhere, six Indian tourists who ignored security warnings

00:05:27.554 --> 00:05:33.694
in Nepal required rescue during a trek. Bulgaria holds a presidential runoff focused on Ukraine ties,

00:05:34.134 --> 00:05:39.465
with voters choosing between candidates who differ on Russia and the war. To really understand

00:05:39.465 --> 00:05:44.445
how a strike on one tanker can lift energy costs for utilities and factories far from the water,

00:05:44.925 --> 00:05:50.545
start with the straight of hormones as a choke in the pipe, not a local accident. Roughly one fifth

00:05:50.545 --> 00:05:55.405
of global oil and a growing share of liquefied natural gas has to pass that narrow stretch.

00:05:55.405 --> 00:06:03.845
Tankers cannot easily reroute because alternative paths add weeks and require different vessel types or port infrastructure that many buyers lack.

00:06:04.445 --> 00:06:09.765
Buyers without the right ports or ship classes cannot simply switch routes the way a truck can switch highways.

00:06:10.305 --> 00:06:13.985
When one carrier is struck, insurers raise premiums across the route.

00:06:14.465 --> 00:06:19.825
Those higher premiums directly lift delivered prices for utilities and manufacturers far from the incident.

00:06:19.825 --> 00:06:22.945
The price signal does not wait for a full shut down.

00:06:23.445 --> 00:06:27.685
Slower transits and fatter insurance bills are enough to move what households and plants

00:06:27.685 --> 00:06:28.045
pay.

00:06:28.685 --> 00:06:33.185
Historical parallels show that even temporary closures or speed reductions in the straight

00:06:33.185 --> 00:06:37.365
have produced measurable spikes in European and Asian energy costs within days.

00:06:38.085 --> 00:06:43.045
Coverage often treats each tanker incident as a one-off when the cost travels through insurance

00:06:43.045 --> 00:06:46.485
and routing markets whether or not a single haul is badly damaged.

00:06:46.485 --> 00:06:51.405
When the next tanker headline lands, check the daily vessel counts that week from the

00:06:51.405 --> 00:06:56.505
International Maritime Organization or UK Maritime Trade Operations, rather than

00:06:56.505 --> 00:06:58.805
judging the route by any single ship in the frame.

00:06:59.877 --> 00:07:04.297
Al Jazeera frames the strike as part of a wartime campaign against commercial shipping through

00:07:04.297 --> 00:07:08.957
the strait, while Bloomberg frames it around a cargo that had already been cleared for passage

00:07:08.957 --> 00:07:09.997
and was hit anyway.

00:07:10.557 --> 00:07:16.097
The past seven days left three files open, an Israeli election, a Spanish rail crash, and

00:07:16.097 --> 00:07:22.577
suspected theft at Binance. 7.3 million Israelis voted in an election that could end Netanyahu's

00:07:22.577 --> 00:07:28.157
rule after three years of war. At least 10 people died when two high-speed trains collided in Central

00:07:28.157 --> 00:07:34.617
Spain, suspending services between Madrid and Seville. Binance suffered a suspected 6.3 billion

00:07:34.617 --> 00:07:40.597
dollar hack, putting crypto holdings of users worldwide at risk. Monday's meeting of China's central

00:07:40.597 --> 00:07:44.817
bank and securities regulator will show which capital market tools they actually put

00:07:44.817 --> 00:07:45.217
to work.

00:07:45.757 --> 00:07:46.697
That's omniview.

00:07:47.157 --> 00:07:51.077
The news can feel heavy, but understanding what's actually happening and what's being

00:07:51.077 --> 00:07:53.697
done about it beats doom scrolling every time.

00:07:54.397 --> 00:07:58.877
Stay curious, pick one story from today and read it from a second outlet you don't usually

00:07:58.877 --> 00:07:59.257
open.

00:07:59.837 --> 00:08:04.137
If balanced perspectives are valuable to you, share this with a friend and subscribe wherever

00:08:04.137 --> 00:08:04.717
you listen.

